1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:01,210
It's 3:07 a.m.

2
00:00:01,230 --> 00:00:04,740
You're alone on the night shift at a
highway gas station.

3
00:00:04,930 --> 00:00:06,630
Then the door chime rings...

4
00:00:06,650 --> 00:00:10,230
and whatever just walked in is
not here for gas.

5
00:00:10,490 --> 00:00:12,070
You slam the lockdown button.

6
00:00:12,090 --> 00:00:13,930
Steel shutters crash down.

7
00:00:14,270 --> 00:00:15,050
Day one.

8
00:00:15,070 --> 00:00:16,390
Twenty-nine to go.

9
00:00:16,880 --> 00:00:22,100
You have one small store, one steel shutter, and
thousands of gallons of fuel under

10
00:00:22,120 --> 00:00:26,020
your feet that every survivor in this
county is about to want.

11
00:00:26,210 --> 00:00:29,210
To reach Day 30, you'll have to
solve five problems.

12
00:00:29,230 --> 00:00:32,510
And one of them nearly kills
you on Day 19.

13
00:00:37,530 --> 00:00:38,310
Day one.

14
00:00:38,330 --> 00:00:42,230
The adrenaline wears off around sunrise, and
your hands start shaking.

15
00:00:42,530 --> 00:00:45,450
Problem one: you don't actually
know what you have.

16
00:00:45,470 --> 00:00:48,010
So before anything clever, you count.

17
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:49,850
Six cases of bottled water.

18
00:00:49,870 --> 00:00:51,520
Four hundred bags of chips.

19
00:00:51,540 --> 00:00:52,773
Two hot dog rollers.

20
00:00:52,793 --> 00:00:53,906
One first aid kit.

21
00:00:53,926 --> 00:00:58,640
And a coffee machine that won't save your
life, but might save your mind.

22
00:00:58,820 --> 00:01:00,880
Water is the real clock.

23
00:01:00,900 --> 00:01:04,520
FEMA says plan on one gallon per
person, per day.

24
00:01:04,570 --> 00:01:08,150
Six cases is about nineteen gallons.

25
00:01:08,350 --> 00:01:09,650
Nineteen days.

26
00:01:09,670 --> 00:01:10,930
Remember that number.

27
00:01:11,350 --> 00:01:13,841
Then you notice the second problem.

28
00:01:13,861 --> 00:01:16,701
The sign outside still glows: OPEN 24/7.

29
00:01:16,721 --> 00:01:20,090
In a dead town, that sign is a
dinner bell.

30
00:01:20,250 --> 00:01:21,450
You pull the breaker.

31
00:01:21,470 --> 00:01:22,590
The sign dies.

32
00:01:22,730 --> 00:01:26,530
And somewhere in the dark, something
stops walking toward you.

33
00:01:26,620 --> 00:01:29,980
Then you drag every shelf you can lift
against the back door.

34
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:31,360
The shutter covers the front.

35
00:01:31,380 --> 00:01:32,940
Nothing covers the back.

36
00:01:33,100 --> 00:01:37,940
New rule of the night shift: no lights, no
noise, and nobody comes in.

37
00:01:41,330 --> 00:01:42,084
Day three.

38
00:01:42,104 --> 00:01:45,290
At 2:14 in the afternoon, the hum stops.

39
00:01:45,720 --> 00:01:46,660
The fridges.

40
00:01:46,680 --> 00:01:47,320
The lights.

41
00:01:47,420 --> 00:01:48,340
The ice machine.

42
00:01:48,360 --> 00:01:50,980
The grid is gone, and it isn't
coming back.

43
00:01:51,180 --> 00:01:55,340
Inside, it's suddenly so quiet you can
hear your own heartbeat.

44
00:01:55,690 --> 00:01:58,630
Problem three: your food just
started a countdown.

45
00:01:58,670 --> 00:02:03,630
Food safety officials say a closed fridge keeps
food safe for about four hours.

46
00:02:03,670 --> 00:02:05,750
A full freezer, about forty-eight.

47
00:02:06,030 --> 00:02:07,450
So you eat in order.

48
00:02:07,470 --> 00:02:08,870
Hot dogs and milk first.

49
00:02:08,930 --> 00:02:09,930
Sandwiches next.

50
00:02:09,950 --> 00:02:11,850
Chips and canned food, last.

51
00:02:12,180 --> 00:02:16,420
On aisle three you find a camping lantern
and forty-eight batteries.

52
00:02:16,460 --> 00:02:19,560
Light, but only the kind that never
leaves the building.

53
00:02:19,770 --> 00:02:24,475
And you find the strongest room in the building:
the walk-in cooler behind the drink

54
00:02:24,495 --> 00:02:24,864
doors.

55
00:02:24,884 --> 00:02:25,587
Thick walls.

56
00:02:25,607 --> 00:02:26,143
One door.

57
00:02:26,163 --> 00:02:27,130
No windows.

58
00:02:27,520 --> 00:02:31,100
You don't know it yet, but that room is
going to save your life.

59
00:02:31,570 --> 00:02:34,150
That night, you hear them for
the first time.

60
00:02:34,170 --> 00:02:34,890
Not one.

61
00:02:34,910 --> 00:02:35,470
Dozens.

62
00:02:39,140 --> 00:02:39,877
Day seven.

63
00:02:39,897 --> 00:02:40,566
4:40 a.m.

64
00:02:40,586 --> 00:02:44,260
A car alarm starts screaming in
the parking lot.

65
00:02:44,430 --> 00:02:45,850
You didn't set it off.

66
00:02:45,870 --> 00:02:47,430
Something walked into it.

67
00:02:47,450 --> 00:02:50,730
And everything within a mile just heard
the dinner bell again.

68
00:02:50,950 --> 00:02:55,070
By sunrise, there are forty of them
pressed against your shutter.

69
00:02:55,390 --> 00:02:56,290
Forty bodies.

70
00:02:56,310 --> 00:03:00,230
Six thousand pounds of weight against
one sheet of steel.

71
00:03:00,250 --> 00:03:01,210
The shutter bends.

72
00:03:01,230 --> 00:03:02,470
One bolt pops.

73
00:03:02,490 --> 00:03:03,610
Then another.

74
00:03:03,850 --> 00:03:06,650
This is where most people make
their first mistake.

75
00:03:06,670 --> 00:03:07,470
They panic.

76
00:03:07,550 --> 00:03:08,470
They make noise.

77
00:03:08,530 --> 00:03:09,670
They try to run.

78
00:03:09,890 --> 00:03:11,110
You do the opposite.

79
00:03:11,350 --> 00:03:11,950
Shoes off.

80
00:03:11,970 --> 00:03:12,650
Lights off.

81
00:03:12,670 --> 00:03:15,010
You crawl behind the counter, and
you don't move.

82
00:03:15,030 --> 00:03:16,670
For eleven hours.

83
00:03:17,140 --> 00:03:22,080
Rule of the night shift: silence is the only
weapon that never runs out.

84
00:03:22,340 --> 00:03:25,060
By nightfall they drift away, one by one.

85
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:28,220
And then, on the night of Day 12,
someone knocks.

86
00:03:28,260 --> 00:03:29,160
Not a scratch.

87
00:03:29,240 --> 00:03:29,880
A knock.

88
00:03:29,900 --> 00:03:30,840
Three times.

89
00:03:34,400 --> 00:03:39,120
Every highway gas station has a night window: a
steel drawer for passing cigarettes

90
00:03:39,140 --> 00:03:40,860
to customers after midnight.

91
00:03:41,160 --> 00:03:42,480
The knock comes again.

92
00:03:42,500 --> 00:03:46,300
You crawl to the window, and you slide
the drawer open one inch.

93
00:03:46,620 --> 00:03:48,480
Tonight, a voice comes through it.

94
00:03:48,500 --> 00:03:49,140
A woman.

95
00:03:49,160 --> 00:03:49,980
Trucker jacket.

96
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:50,600
Hands up.

97
00:03:50,620 --> 00:03:51,240
'Please.

98
00:03:51,280 --> 00:03:52,220
I'm not bitten.'

99
00:03:52,520 --> 00:03:53,500
Her name is Dee.

100
00:03:53,520 --> 00:03:55,960
Her truck jackknifed a mile
down the highway.

101
00:03:55,980 --> 00:03:57,520
And she has news.

102
00:03:57,820 --> 00:04:01,980
The radio says the National Guard will run an
evacuation point at the county

103
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:02,300
stadium.

104
00:04:02,320 --> 00:04:03,600
Eighteen days from now.

105
00:04:03,620 --> 00:04:04,880
Six miles away.

106
00:04:05,050 --> 00:04:07,050
Problem four isn't zombies.

107
00:04:07,190 --> 00:04:08,050
It's people.

108
00:04:08,090 --> 00:04:09,990
Open the door, and you get a partner...

109
00:04:10,010 --> 00:04:12,730
or someone who takes everything you have.

110
00:04:12,950 --> 00:04:13,890
What would you do?

111
00:04:13,910 --> 00:04:14,510
Think about it.

112
00:04:14,530 --> 00:04:16,410
Because you don't open the door.

113
00:04:16,730 --> 00:04:19,730
You slide two bottles of water through
the drawer instead.

114
00:04:19,770 --> 00:04:20,430
She nods...

115
00:04:20,450 --> 00:04:22,210
and walks back into the rain.

116
00:04:22,360 --> 00:04:23,800
You'll see her again.

117
00:04:23,820 --> 00:04:26,100
And next time, she won't be alone.

118
00:04:29,620 --> 00:04:30,620
Day fifteen.

119
00:04:30,780 --> 00:04:33,060
Boredom is its own kind of danger.

120
00:04:33,100 --> 00:04:34,920
So you give your brain a job.

121
00:04:34,940 --> 00:04:35,840
You watch them.

122
00:04:35,970 --> 00:04:39,370
Through a crack in the shutter, with a notebook
from the register, you write down

123
00:04:39,390 --> 00:04:40,710
everything they do.

124
00:04:40,790 --> 00:04:42,390
They don't see well in the dark.

125
00:04:42,410 --> 00:04:44,210
They follow sound for miles.

126
00:04:44,290 --> 00:04:48,890
And every evening at six, about twenty of them
drift down the highway like a tide.

127
00:04:49,130 --> 00:04:50,710
Patterns are survival.

128
00:04:50,730 --> 00:04:53,470
If you know when they come, you know
when you can move.

129
00:04:53,700 --> 00:04:55,820
And you learn one more thing.

130
00:04:55,840 --> 00:04:58,360
The loudest sound always wins.

131
00:04:58,380 --> 00:04:59,620
Remember that, too.

132
00:05:02,970 --> 00:05:03,930
Day nineteen.

133
00:05:03,950 --> 00:05:04,990
Remember that number?

134
00:05:05,010 --> 00:05:06,610
The last bottle is empty.

135
00:05:06,970 --> 00:05:09,630
But you didn't skip the boring
part of survival.

136
00:05:09,650 --> 00:05:14,150
FEMA lists a hidden water source in almost
every building: the water heater.

137
00:05:14,380 --> 00:05:16,740
Forty gallons, sitting in the back room.

138
00:05:16,760 --> 00:05:18,200
You open the drain valve.

139
00:05:18,220 --> 00:05:19,120
Clean water.

140
00:05:19,140 --> 00:05:20,140
Weeks more.

141
00:05:20,160 --> 00:05:22,100
You almost laugh.

142
00:05:22,590 --> 00:05:23,892
And that's the mistake.

143
00:05:23,912 --> 00:05:27,693
To reach the valve, you dragged the shelves
away from the back door.

144
00:05:27,713 --> 00:05:29,390
You never put them back.

145
00:05:29,790 --> 00:05:30,230
3 a.m.

146
00:05:30,250 --> 00:05:32,006
The back door clicks open.

147
00:05:32,026 --> 00:05:34,430
The latch was broken all along.

148
00:05:34,730 --> 00:05:36,170
There's one of them inside.

149
00:05:36,250 --> 00:05:38,830
Between you and everything you own.

150
00:05:39,060 --> 00:05:41,044
You run for the strongest room you have.

151
00:05:41,064 --> 00:05:42,021
The walk-in cooler.

152
00:05:42,041 --> 00:05:44,100
You pull the door shut and hold it.

153
00:05:44,250 --> 00:05:48,650
Now you're sealed in the dark, your breath turning
to fog, listening to it scratch

154
00:05:48,670 --> 00:05:49,690
at the door.

155
00:05:50,040 --> 00:05:52,420
On your belt is the cashier's handset.

156
00:05:52,440 --> 00:05:56,540
It's wired to the speakers outside, the ones
that say 'pump four is ready.'

157
00:05:56,750 --> 00:05:59,650
You press the button, and you bang
it against the wall.

158
00:05:59,880 --> 00:06:00,600
It turns.

159
00:06:00,720 --> 00:06:03,560
It follows the sound, out the back
door, into the rain.

160
00:06:03,580 --> 00:06:07,300
You sprint, slam the door, and bury it
under every shelf you own.

161
00:06:07,530 --> 00:06:09,450
You survived your mistake.

162
00:06:09,470 --> 00:06:13,230
But you just told the whole county
exactly where you are.

163
00:06:16,610 --> 00:06:17,890
Day twenty-four.

164
00:06:18,010 --> 00:06:18,710
Headlights.

165
00:06:19,150 --> 00:06:20,530
A pickup truck rolls in.

166
00:06:20,550 --> 00:06:21,250
Three men.

167
00:06:21,270 --> 00:06:22,390
Empty gas cans.

168
00:06:22,410 --> 00:06:23,730
And in the passenger seat...

169
00:06:23,750 --> 00:06:24,230
Dee.

170
00:06:24,520 --> 00:06:29,120
Problem five: the pumps are dead without power,
and they think you know how to turn

171
00:06:29,140 --> 00:06:29,840
them on.

172
00:06:30,050 --> 00:06:31,430
They pound on the shutter.

173
00:06:31,450 --> 00:06:33,490
'Open up, and nobody gets hurt.'

174
00:06:33,670 --> 00:06:35,830
One of them jams a crowbar
under the shutter.

175
00:06:35,850 --> 00:06:37,010
Metal screams.

176
00:06:37,130 --> 00:06:38,330
You watch the gap grow.

177
00:06:38,350 --> 00:06:39,070
Two inches.

178
00:06:39,090 --> 00:06:39,650
Four.

179
00:06:39,900 --> 00:06:40,880
You don't answer.

180
00:06:40,900 --> 00:06:43,440
Rule of the night shift: nobody comes in.

181
00:06:43,670 --> 00:06:46,530
And their noise does what noise
always does.

182
00:06:46,550 --> 00:06:51,390
Forty shapes walk out of the trees, toward the
loudest thing in the parking lot.

183
00:06:51,550 --> 00:06:52,630
Engines roar.

184
00:06:52,650 --> 00:06:53,790
Tires scream.

185
00:06:53,810 --> 00:06:54,890
And they're gone.

186
00:06:55,220 --> 00:06:57,620
Dee looks back at your store
through the rain.

187
00:06:57,640 --> 00:06:59,360
You'll never know if she was
their prisoner...

188
00:06:59,380 --> 00:07:00,580
or their guide.

189
00:07:04,050 --> 00:07:04,830
Day thirty.

190
00:07:04,850 --> 00:07:07,190
You scratch the last mark into
the shutter.

191
00:07:07,230 --> 00:07:08,170
Thirty lines.

192
00:07:08,190 --> 00:07:10,830
Thirty mornings you were never
supposed to see.

193
00:07:11,040 --> 00:07:13,060
You counted before you acted.

194
00:07:13,080 --> 00:07:14,380
You killed the light.

195
00:07:14,420 --> 00:07:15,620
You stayed silent.

196
00:07:15,640 --> 00:07:16,960
You found the hidden water.

197
00:07:16,980 --> 00:07:19,080
And you never opened the door.

198
00:07:19,370 --> 00:07:21,130
The evacuation is tomorrow.

199
00:07:21,170 --> 00:07:24,830
Six miles of highway, on foot, with
everything you can carry.

200
00:07:25,090 --> 00:07:28,850
Before you go, you leave a note on the
counter for whoever comes next.

201
00:07:28,870 --> 00:07:29,370
Count.

202
00:07:29,390 --> 00:07:30,230
Stay dark.

203
00:07:30,250 --> 00:07:31,190
Stay quiet.

204
00:07:31,210 --> 00:07:32,390
Don't open the door.

205
00:07:32,550 --> 00:07:38,910
You're packing your bag when, at exactly 3:07
a.m., the lights flicker on.

206
00:07:39,100 --> 00:07:40,330
Every one of them.

207
00:07:40,350 --> 00:07:43,029
The sign outside glows again: OPEN 24/7.

208
00:07:43,049 --> 00:07:45,060
And the door chime rings.

209
00:07:45,530 --> 00:07:47,450
Somebody turned the power back on.

210
00:07:47,470 --> 00:07:50,670
And somebody knows you're still in here.

211
00:07:51,350 --> 00:07:53,130
Would you have opened the window for Dee?

212
00:07:53,150 --> 00:07:53,830
Tell me in the comments.

213
00:07:53,850 --> 00:07:57,750
And subscribe, because Day 31
starts right now.

